<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kim Ryholt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1970">1970</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kim Ryholt is a Danish Egyptologist at the University of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copenhagen">Copenhagen</a>, known for his work on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-intermediate-period">Second Intermediate Period</a> and on demotic literature. In his 1997 study of the period he proposed that a group of kings in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turin-king-list">Turin King List</a> formed a local Abydos Dynasty around 1650 BCE, a view supported by the discovery of the tomb of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senebkay">Senebkay</a> in 2014.</p></div>
